WEBVTT

00:13.740 --> 00:14.970
<i>What's the situation?!</i>

00:14.970 --> 00:18.490
<i>It's chaotic with emergency 
vehicles and evacuees.</i>

00:18.490 --> 00:20.540
<i>A terrorist bombing in the state capital?!</i>

00:20.540 --> 00:22.610
<i>What do they think they're doing?</i>

00:23.010 --> 00:26.250
This bombing could be a diversion.

00:26.250 --> 00:29.130
Surely you're not saying... There's no way!

00:29.130 --> 00:33.130
This is going down right as the three princes
 are making a public appearance.

00:39.760 --> 00:44.320
But I gotta say... Catching terrorists
 isn't a car dealer's job, you know?

00:44.320 --> 00:47.270
<i>Since players are involved,</i>

00:47.270 --> 00:49.010
it is very much so our job.

00:49.650 --> 00:52.030
Find them and collect the cards.

00:52.030 --> 00:52.980
<i>Roger.</i>

00:52.980 --> 00:54.280
Roger.

00:58.440 --> 00:59.660
Who are you?

01:01.050 --> 01:02.540
Goodbye.

01:09.540 --> 01:11.920
Leo, I found some suspicious guys.

01:11.920 --> 01:13.540
It's probably them.

01:14.380 --> 01:16.780
Okay, okay. That's enough running.

01:16.780 --> 01:18.890
Playing tag is exhausting.

01:18.890 --> 01:19.890
Play.

01:31.070 --> 01:32.910
<i>Chris, are you okay?</i>

01:33.220 --> 01:34.150
<i>What about the card?</i>

01:34.150 --> 01:36.230
Sorry, it got away.

01:53.200 --> 01:55.840
I am so blind

01:55.840 --> 01:57.840
Still running

01:58.120 --> 02:01.060
Running out of sight

02:01.060 --> 02:02.710
In the night

02:02.710 --> 02:05.220
I'm feeling goosebumps

02:06.590 --> 02:13.690
Betting against the odds again,
I'm being swayed like in a dance

02:13.690 --> 02:18.360
No more Blah Blah Bluff-filled Table

02:19.970 --> 02:21.850
Just tell me how to figure it out

02:21.850 --> 02:23.660
Inside my head, I'm painting the town

02:23.660 --> 02:24.870
Addition is affliction

02:24.870 --> 02:25.740
Something's missing

02:25.740 --> 02:27.560
(Oh you really got me wrong)

02:27.560 --> 02:29.420
I wanna get out so I'm taking a chance

02:29.420 --> 02:30.280
I gotta advance

02:30.280 --> 02:31.470
You know who I am?

02:31.470 --> 02:32.920
I'm a trickster

02:33.790 --> 02:35.380
Just take a chance

02:35.380 --> 02:36.550
Play the game

02:36.550 --> 02:38.550
It sounds insane

02:38.550 --> 02:41.720
Fate smiles at the borderline

02:41.720 --> 02:48.060
Rather than dance to someone else's tune,
I wanna dance to my own.

02:48.060 --> 02:50.020
Yea I'm moving like that

02:50.020 --> 02:51.320
Give it a try

02:51.320 --> 02:52.440
Keep on going down

02:52.440 --> 02:55.120
I just need something real

02:55.120 --> 02:58.690
Then we need no fakes

02:58.690 --> 03:02.950
I'll let my soul be wild and free

03:17.690 --> 03:20.670
<i>And now, more on the terrorist bombing.</i>

03:20.670 --> 03:24.740
<i>The unexpected tragedy took place at the
Royal Museum's bicentennial ceremony,</i>

03:24.740 --> 03:31.060
<i>where First Prince Dylan, 
Second Prince Louis, and Third Prince Noah</i>

03:31.350 --> 03:33.810
<i>were all in attendance.</i>

03:33.810 --> 03:38.820
<i>It is with deep regret and great sorrow
that we report Prince Dylan,</i>

03:38.820 --> 03:43.240
<i>who was to be coronated in three months,
did not survive the attack.</i>

03:43.820 --> 03:46.950
<i>No one has claimed responsibility
 for the bombing yet,</i>

03:46.950 --> 03:51.910
<i>and the city is on high alert
due to the baffling situation.</i>

03:54.140 --> 03:56.840
There's a gag order on the media,

03:57.290 --> 04:01.390
but eyewitnesses are talking
 about sudden blasts out of nowhere

04:01.850 --> 04:04.790
and iron and stone walls attacking them.

04:05.210 --> 04:07.650
That's not for us to worry about.

04:07.650 --> 04:09.010
This again?!

04:09.010 --> 04:13.100
People with bizarre powers are committing
 bizarre crimes all over the city.

04:13.100 --> 04:16.210
If we can't investigate, 
then what good are the police?!

04:16.210 --> 04:18.230
We're supposed to uphold the law!

04:22.450 --> 04:26.040
I just want the truth.

04:27.670 --> 04:29.690
There are things you're better off not knowing.

04:34.530 --> 04:37.750
My sincerest condolences, Your Majesty.

04:37.750 --> 04:41.010
Theodore, was this incident...

04:41.010 --> 04:44.070
Yes, it's just as Your Majesty suspects.

04:45.090 --> 04:49.150
The bloody struggle that surrounds
 the X-Playing Cards...

04:49.150 --> 04:53.820
It has repeated many times 
throughout the history of Fourland

04:53.820 --> 04:57.650
every time the cards fall
into the hands of the heartless.

04:57.650 --> 05:03.710
That is why the cards must be contained 
for the peace of this country.

05:05.320 --> 05:09.030
Their powers are far too great
 for humans to handle.

05:10.970 --> 05:13.000
We're a little tired.

05:13.000 --> 05:14.420
Let us return to our chamber.

05:16.990 --> 05:18.290
Listen well.

05:18.750 --> 05:22.800
The cards must never take center stage.

05:28.330 --> 05:30.790
Why the long face?

05:31.900 --> 05:34.460
Ban... Why are you here?

05:34.460 --> 05:37.190
To pay my respects, of course.

05:37.190 --> 05:39.240
How awfully commendable of you.

05:39.650 --> 05:42.470
Did you want to see me in trouble that badly?

05:42.470 --> 05:45.970
Oh, yes. You look precious, Theodore.

05:47.270 --> 05:49.480
Why did you kill Prince Dylan?

05:49.480 --> 05:52.950
Must you show off your power so?

05:53.270 --> 05:55.640
Cards are meant to be played.

05:55.640 --> 05:58.060
Isn't it more fun this way?

05:58.060 --> 06:02.340
Putting it all on the table.
 Absolutely everything.

06:02.340 --> 06:05.160
You should put your cards down too.

06:06.670 --> 06:09.400
You sound as though
 you think you have a chance.

06:12.260 --> 06:14.590
There's no being in the right here.

06:14.900 --> 06:17.730
You should know that better than anyone.

06:18.840 --> 06:22.140
It's a matter of pride.

06:33.160 --> 06:35.310
Assemble High Card immediately.

06:55.350 --> 06:56.210
Hello?

06:56.750 --> 06:58.220
<i>A job for you.</i>

06:58.220 --> 07:01.290
<i>All members of High Card have been summoned.</i>

07:01.650 --> 07:05.270
<i>Could you please come to the store?</i>

07:05.580 --> 07:07.540
All members? Including Finn?

07:07.850 --> 07:11.160
<i>Finn isn't answering his phone.</i>

07:13.750 --> 07:15.580
<i>It's been two weeks now.</i>

07:15.580 --> 07:16.840
<i>I'm concerned.</i>

07:18.100 --> 07:19.470
<i>I'll be waiting for you.</i>

07:19.470 --> 07:20.750
Understood.

07:29.510 --> 07:32.180
Thank you for coming.
 I believe you know why you're all here.

07:32.490 --> 07:37.400
Master Theodore called with an order.
We are to retrieve any cards

07:37.400 --> 07:40.060
with known whereabouts effective immediately.

07:40.060 --> 07:41.570
The president ordered that?

07:41.570 --> 07:43.460
But why so suddenly?

07:43.460 --> 07:46.690
I'm sure the situation is that dire.

07:47.310 --> 07:50.900
It wouldn't be an exaggeration to say
we're in a state of emergency.

07:51.330 --> 07:57.910
Vijay, Wendy, you two go to Silphium. 
Master Leo, you shall go to Neville.

07:58.220 --> 08:01.280
Remember, the whereabouts of these 
cards are highly confidential.

08:01.280 --> 08:03.320
No one else can find out.

08:03.730 --> 08:05.540
Especially <i>them</i>.

08:05.540 --> 08:07.500
The Klondikes...

08:07.500 --> 08:11.540
Yesterday's attack was most likely
the doing of their players, wasn't it?

08:12.110 --> 08:14.590
Speculating at this point will do us no good.

08:14.590 --> 08:16.270
I'd like you two to take these.

08:16.610 --> 08:18.850
You should hurry a bit.

08:19.820 --> 08:21.580
The train leaves in an hour?!

08:21.580 --> 08:23.400
We've gotta go, Vijay!

08:23.400 --> 08:26.380
But I don't have my usual overnight kit...

08:26.380 --> 08:27.940
Who cares about that?!

08:28.300 --> 08:29.390
Master Leo?

08:29.390 --> 08:30.520
I'll be fine.

08:30.520 --> 08:32.320
I understand the mission.

08:32.320 --> 08:36.290
Chris, you will go to Polostick with Finn.

08:36.690 --> 08:39.580
Please take the last train today.

08:39.580 --> 08:42.210
With Finn? But he's...

08:42.730 --> 08:47.690
I know he's deeply saddened and hurt 
after losing a place he called home.

08:47.690 --> 08:51.960
But there's no reason you can only have
 one home sweet home.

08:51.960 --> 08:55.350
I didn't sign up to be his babysitter.

08:56.150 --> 09:00.080
You two are buddies. You make a pair.

09:00.080 --> 09:02.460
I'm just his mentor.

09:10.660 --> 09:14.050
<i>Please take care of Finn.</i>

09:17.860 --> 09:19.890
A place to call home, huh?

09:51.240 --> 09:52.380
Listen, Finn.

09:52.870 --> 09:54.780
Starting today, this is your home.

09:55.860 --> 09:58.780
I know your parents were 
in a terrible accident,

09:59.370 --> 10:03.080
but now, everyone at Sun Fields 
will be your new family.

10:03.830 --> 10:10.540
In truth, I'd be much happier 
if you didn't come back here at all.

10:17.050 --> 10:19.430
Are you alive, Finn?

10:20.830 --> 10:22.180
Leave me alone.

10:22.400 --> 10:24.300
Oh, you are alive.

10:25.000 --> 10:27.860
Old man Bernard called you, didn't he?

10:27.860 --> 10:28.970
We got a job.

10:28.970 --> 10:29.940
A job?

10:31.430 --> 10:33.850
Working's pointless now.

10:34.200 --> 10:37.350
No matter how much money I make, 
Sun Fields will never...

10:39.620 --> 10:41.810
My memories are hazy too.

10:42.210 --> 10:44.450
And so... I'm...

10:44.930 --> 10:45.750
I can't...

10:49.140 --> 10:50.240
Listen, Finn...

10:51.590 --> 10:54.960
Is what happened in the past 
really that big of a deal?

10:56.170 --> 10:58.990
You have no idea what I'm going through.

10:59.370 --> 11:01.390
Well, you're not wrong there.

11:03.140 --> 11:06.230
I don't have a real family anymore.

11:06.850 --> 11:09.150
I trusted Lindsey, but he lied to me...

11:09.740 --> 11:11.690
It doesn't have to be family.

11:11.690 --> 11:16.130
Whether it's a lover, a friend,
or even an acquaintance...

11:17.090 --> 11:21.260
As long as someone's with you,
you're not alone, right?

11:22.740 --> 11:24.180
That's just quibbling.

11:24.180 --> 11:25.090
Maybe.

11:26.140 --> 11:27.410
But I'm saying, Finn,

11:28.200 --> 11:32.510
that the least I can do is 
stick with you from time to time.

11:33.550 --> 11:35.670
That way, you won't be alone.

11:37.870 --> 11:43.220
The old man says we're buddies.
That the two of us make a pair.

11:44.330 --> 11:45.680
Isn't that hilarious?

11:45.680 --> 11:46.670
Buddies?

11:47.240 --> 11:48.970
We're just colleagues.

11:50.150 --> 11:51.060
I know, right?

11:52.970 --> 11:53.810
Say, Finn.

11:54.190 --> 12:00.370
You have to stop thinking, 
"If not for me..." or, "If I hadn't been there..."

12:00.750 --> 12:02.370
If you put yourself in that position,

12:02.370 --> 12:07.350
you'll get to feeling like nothing 
matters and do something stupid.

12:08.370 --> 12:10.200
And the truth is, Finn...

12:11.320 --> 12:13.350
I don't want you to end up that way.

12:16.210 --> 12:19.380
It wasn't your fault. 
That's all I came to say.

12:20.340 --> 12:24.050
Anyhoo, I can handle this job myself.

12:24.530 --> 12:25.540
See ya.

12:25.540 --> 12:27.350
Make sure you get plenty of calories!

12:42.280 --> 12:43.570
Chris...

12:50.040 --> 12:53.790
Nhât used us and took credit for everything.

12:53.790 --> 12:55.670
That really pisses me off!

12:55.670 --> 12:59.470
We're Klondike Family players too, you know?!

13:01.010 --> 13:02.910
Damn it, I'm so pissed!

13:02.910 --> 13:04.510
Yeah, I'm pissed.

13:04.510 --> 13:06.650
Let's do it! We're really gonna do it!

13:06.650 --> 13:07.640
Right, Alex?!

13:07.890 --> 13:09.260
Yeah, we will.

13:11.240 --> 13:12.980
Okay, where's the menu?

13:12.980 --> 13:15.020
Here you go!

13:15.020 --> 13:16.490
You fellas wanna order more?

13:19.620 --> 13:21.070
Is this for us?

13:21.070 --> 13:23.080
Huh? What is that?

13:24.810 --> 13:26.180
This must be...

13:30.370 --> 13:33.640
I hope this allows for even 
the slightest bit of progress.

13:36.350 --> 13:39.950
Here you go. 
Three Fudgees and one orange juice.

13:39.950 --> 13:41.840
Oh, and don't forget this.

13:42.390 --> 13:43.420
Sure thing.

13:47.100 --> 13:52.100
<i>The sleeper train Occidental, bound 
for Acorn Field, will depart soon.</i>

13:52.100 --> 13:54.310
<i>Passengers are advised to board immediately.</i>

13:59.530 --> 14:00.840
I made it!

14:01.290 --> 14:03.700
Finn... You sure you're up for this?

14:03.700 --> 14:06.620
Yup! I got plenty of calories, so I'm good.

14:06.620 --> 14:08.820
Come on. Let's get on, Chris.

14:10.860 --> 14:11.670
Sure.

14:22.350 --> 14:25.180
Aya Tawawa, age 48.

14:25.180 --> 14:27.590
She's in possession of the jack of clubs,

14:27.590 --> 14:30.060
with a power called "Coming Home."

14:30.810 --> 14:32.600
So this is who we're up against?

14:32.840 --> 14:35.460
Yup, she's our target.

14:36.030 --> 14:39.100
By the way... why did you decide to come?

14:42.230 --> 14:45.730
Chris, you said we were buddies.

14:49.990 --> 14:51.650
I was scared.

14:51.650 --> 14:54.470
I blamed myself for what
 happened to Sun Fields.

14:54.950 --> 14:59.370
Because of me, the important 
place I wanted to protect was...

14:59.720 --> 15:07.130
Ever since that day, I've felt like 
just moving would destroy me, so...

15:09.660 --> 15:14.730
But you told me it wasn't my fault.

15:15.170 --> 15:18.020
And then I could move again.

15:18.020 --> 15:20.810
Even though "just a colleague" said it?

15:20.810 --> 15:22.230
Put a sock in it.

15:22.870 --> 15:26.480
As long as I keep moving,
I don't have to think about anything else.

15:26.480 --> 15:29.670
Because I don't have a home to go back to.

15:30.230 --> 15:32.340
You can go home anytime.

15:32.340 --> 15:34.380
I'm sure Lindsey is waiting for you.

15:34.380 --> 15:37.240
He said it'd be better if I didn't come back.

15:37.240 --> 15:37.790
What?

15:38.700 --> 15:42.810
I earned all that money for him, and yet...

15:44.110 --> 15:48.130
Let me tell you something 
as your mentor, little baby Finn.

15:48.390 --> 15:50.650
Adults are complicated.

15:50.650 --> 15:54.780
You have to get what goes into what they
 say in order to get your head around 'em.

15:54.780 --> 15:56.410
What's that mean?

15:56.410 --> 15:58.140
You'll understand when you grow up.

16:06.770 --> 16:08.290
Wake up, Finn.

16:08.290 --> 16:09.780
We're almost there.

16:14.070 --> 16:16.290
It's a hike from the station.

16:16.290 --> 16:18.280
I hope we can catch a cab.

16:18.860 --> 16:19.570
Hmm?

16:21.590 --> 16:23.370
Don't get off just yet.

16:23.370 --> 16:25.040
"Metallical Parade"!

16:27.790 --> 16:30.030
A player who wields metal?!

16:30.030 --> 16:31.700
You're that guy from...

16:31.700 --> 16:36.110
I don't know where you're going, 
but we need a word with you.

16:36.110 --> 16:39.180
So quit yapping and get back to your car.

16:39.180 --> 16:41.110
You just said "we."

16:41.430 --> 16:43.310
Is the big guy from the other day with you?

16:43.310 --> 16:44.920
Shut up!

16:44.920 --> 16:47.230
I told you to get moving!

16:52.400 --> 16:54.350
It was just like we were told.

16:54.350 --> 16:57.240
We wait at the station, and you show up.

16:57.240 --> 17:04.500
I don't know who tipped us off, 
but I guess this means we have fans now.

17:04.920 --> 17:09.750
The Klondike Family 
is a bazillion years ahead of you!

17:09.980 --> 17:12.880
Ah, I knew you were a Klondike.

17:13.490 --> 17:16.380
Y-You walked me into that!

17:16.380 --> 17:18.510
You walked into it yourself.

17:18.750 --> 17:24.050
I don't know what you came here for,
 but it doesn't matter!

17:24.050 --> 17:26.110
Your cards! Hand over your cards!

17:26.110 --> 17:30.520
If we turn them over to the boss, 
we'll move up in the family!

17:30.520 --> 17:31.430
That's the idea!

17:31.430 --> 17:32.410
So hurry up and—

17:32.410 --> 17:33.610
Pass.

17:35.870 --> 17:37.410
That's pointless.

17:37.410 --> 17:40.330
You know what my "Calorie's High" does.

17:40.550 --> 17:44.630
But... O-Okay then, how 
about the kid over there?!

17:44.630 --> 17:46.710
Not to mention the passengers.

17:47.180 --> 17:50.960
My partner's gonna drop a ginormous 
rock on the rails at the bridge up ahead.

17:51.320 --> 17:54.360
The train'll crash into it and
 everyone aboard will go splat!

17:54.360 --> 17:56.340
You hear me? Splat!

17:56.610 --> 17:59.420
You'd involve people who've
 got nothing to do with this?!

17:59.420 --> 18:00.050
Huh?

18:00.050 --> 18:03.020
They have nothing to do with <i>you</i>. 
Not a damn thing!

18:03.020 --> 18:05.100
So what do you care?

18:06.490 --> 18:12.150
Now, if you do what I say,
I'll tell Alex not to drop the rock.

18:12.520 --> 18:15.780
Ah, so the guy with 
the 5 of clubs is Alex, huh?

18:15.780 --> 18:17.800
That's Alexander Alekson to you!

18:17.800 --> 18:19.890
You don't get to use his nickname!

18:19.890 --> 18:21.220
Okay, okay.

18:21.220 --> 18:25.060
Can I ask you a question, 
Mr. Friend of Alex's?

18:25.390 --> 18:27.620
Are you joking with me right now?!

18:27.620 --> 18:29.530
I'm Jasper Libera, damn you!

18:29.530 --> 18:31.000
I'm really gonna get mad!

18:31.000 --> 18:32.200
Wow, you're so scary.

18:32.200 --> 18:33.880
H-Hey, Chris...

18:34.120 --> 18:40.390
Now, Jasper, I have to admit using 
the passengers as hostages is a good idea.

18:40.620 --> 18:41.390
I know, right?

18:41.630 --> 18:46.920
But endangering <i>everyone</i>
 on the train includes you, doesn't it?

18:47.550 --> 18:50.130
Come on. I'm sure they thought through—

18:48.890 --> 18:50.830
Shit!

18:50.830 --> 18:53.320
What am I gonna do? You're totally right.

18:53.320 --> 18:54.330
I'm here too.

18:54.330 --> 18:55.900
Damn, this is bad...

18:54.940 --> 18:55.900
Seriously?

18:55.900 --> 18:58.220
There you have it, Finn.

18:58.220 --> 19:00.100
There's nothing behind their threat.

19:03.240 --> 19:06.870
A-Are you saying you don't care 
what happens to the passengers?!

19:07.130 --> 19:11.280
They have nothing to do with me.
So what do I care?

19:11.280 --> 19:12.120
Y'know?

19:12.860 --> 19:14.070
A-Are you serious?

19:14.070 --> 19:17.340
Plus, if you die, I can take your card.

19:17.660 --> 19:19.460
And if I snatch Alex's, that's two.

19:19.460 --> 19:22.260
Th-Then what about him?!

19:23.070 --> 19:27.270
Even if Finn dies,
Pinochle won't be losing a card.

19:27.270 --> 19:31.390
If I get two cards in exchange, 
it's not a bad deal.

19:31.390 --> 19:32.350
You're bluffing!

19:32.350 --> 19:33.490
You can't mean that!

19:33.490 --> 19:35.970
In that case, suit yourself.

19:36.810 --> 19:39.030
Chris, are you serious?

19:39.650 --> 19:42.530
Sorry, Finn. I'm asking you
 to lay down your life.

19:49.740 --> 19:50.700
Here it comes.

19:51.790 --> 19:53.950
C-Crap, we're running out of time.

19:53.950 --> 19:56.280
No, I still have the upper hand.

19:56.280 --> 19:57.020
Give it!

19:57.020 --> 19:59.230
Give me the card and apologize!

19:59.230 --> 20:01.240
You'd better get off the train.

20:01.580 --> 20:02.550
Chris!

20:02.940 --> 20:04.180
The bridge!

20:06.910 --> 20:10.490
Ugh! You're pissing me off!

20:15.650 --> 20:17.170
I won't let you make a fool of me!

20:17.170 --> 20:20.770
Who'll brake first in this game of chicken?!

20:23.510 --> 20:25.970
Play! "G Round"!

20:31.640 --> 20:33.370
Y-You idiot!

20:34.200 --> 20:36.250
Play! "Neo New Nambu"!

20:37.140 --> 20:38.340
That's enough outta you!

20:48.790 --> 20:50.270
You kicked your own friend off.

20:51.670 --> 20:52.560
Whoa!

20:53.150 --> 20:54.700
L-Let me go!

20:54.700 --> 20:55.510
L-Let me...

20:57.770 --> 21:01.030
N-No... Don't let go. Please don't do it.

21:11.870 --> 21:13.530
Are we not gonna make it?

21:14.100 --> 21:17.090
This is bad, this is bad, this is bad...
But I gotta do it!

21:17.090 --> 21:18.880
"Metallical Parade"!

21:19.380 --> 21:21.830
Hot, hot, hot!

21:37.520 --> 21:40.150
I found you, 5 of clubs.

21:42.740 --> 21:44.840
Don't underestimate Jasper Libera.

21:44.840 --> 21:46.070
Just don't!

21:46.070 --> 21:48.450
I'm not gonna let you run amok.

22:05.110 --> 22:09.320
We move on, kicking away a crisis

22:09.320 --> 22:16.740
Dare to cause a dramatic upset

22:18.690 --> 22:23.450
To those of you in the safe zone
who hate to rock the boat

22:23.450 --> 22:26.890
Over here, I'm barely surviving today

22:26.890 --> 22:29.200
In exchange for my MP

22:29.200 --> 22:32.780
I can't cool down this burning passion

22:32.780 --> 22:36.750
Bring it, weak-ass monsters!

22:36.750 --> 22:40.220
With that said, my knees are shaking

22:40.220 --> 22:42.810
But I still dream on

22:42.810 --> 22:46.880
Because I don't want to make myself a liar

22:46.880 --> 22:50.730
(Are you all ready?)

22:49.490 --> 22:51.580
And don't be afraid

22:51.580 --> 22:53.430
Let's get sassy

22:53.430 --> 22:56.720
I'm sharpening the senses I lost

22:56.720 --> 23:00.740
Repeating a desperate act to get in the zone

23:01.650 --> 23:05.950
We move on, welcoming any phenomenon

23:05.950 --> 23:12.140
I challenge myself on the lifeline I run on

23:12.140 --> 23:15.700
Please let it slide if I take a huge tumble

23:15.700 --> 23:20.620
I smile as I go, dedicating my whole life

23:20.620 --> 23:23.460
That's why I get serious

23:23.460 --> 23:25.710
So I can leave my tracks

23:25.710 --> 23:31.930
Shake up the destiny in my hand

23:36.930 --> 23:39.720
Next time: "TO BE APART."
